6068965 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1045 "Finding Intersections of Lines and Reciprocal Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068965 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f7fe334b-af06-545b-8320-d04ce420b4ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1045 "Determining Continuity from Graphs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068989 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "09c8fe50-cab2-5dfd-a90a-5053ffffc1bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1045 "Left and Right Continuity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "acac3ae8-22e4-541d-b0da-b38b7e642d06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069272 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069272 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3471" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069272 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069272 #edb/ref 1071 "The curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ intersects the line $4y-5x=8$ at the points $(p,q)$ and $(r,s).$ What is $p+q+r+s?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069272 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9bdc8c8-a628-5a28-9c53-49f974293c50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069272 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we solve for $y$ in the second curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-5x & =8 \\\\ 4y & =5x+8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{5x+8}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ y=\\frac{5x+8}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the equations equal to one another and solving, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{5x+8}{4} \\\\ 4 & =5{x}^{2}+8x \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+8x-4 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(5x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinates of the intersection points are $x=-2$ and $x=\\frac{2}{5}.$ To find the $y$-coordinates of the intersection points, we plug these values into either curve. Let's choose the first equation.\n\n- Substituting $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso one point of intersection is $(-2,-\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\n- Substituting $x=\\frac{2}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the other point of intersection is $(\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{5}{2}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-2,-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $(\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{5}{2}).$\n\nFinally, if we let $p=-2,q=-\\frac{1}{2},r=\\frac{2}{5}$ and $s=\\frac{5}{2},$ then\n\n$$\np+q+r+s=-2-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nA sketch of the situation is shown below.\n\n![](images/d9/d995288e573a22db67c7d4c82c1a12bcbb41fd880f706b9fb62062aa90e2d5ba.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069312 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069312 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38547" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069312 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069312 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/18/188e0169738a08b3d4580b4f5d3a3ab1aedef87a9d1b83f07c1b10686a38c321.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true in relation to the function $y=g(x)$ above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is continuous at $x=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069312 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f98bb945-e8b3-5349-97c2-0b4b023243ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069312 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=0,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}g(x)=0\\ne -2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=0,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x)=-2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=0,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069567 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069567 #edb/ref 1061 12020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069567 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3561bec4-880a-5815-bc18-84c3d62a3191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069567 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069568 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069568 #edb/ref 1061 12021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069568 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c9dde49-f9f9-5036-8e84-b7e1ced3796b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069568 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069569 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069569 #edb/ref 1061 12022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069569 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "74cd2bd0-c1c2-5429-adda-d13aa18601d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069569 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069570 #edb/ref 1061 12023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069570 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "64c70852-38a7-5f5e-ade8-36856f8eef67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069570 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1061 12117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "27206838-7dfd-50f0-a4b5-a92905b05017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1061 12118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b43b6d85-ec3f-5921-878b-59ca9e5c066f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069573 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069573 